i's GIL around every call (the library's one C thread is shared), so"] [25 1 "//     ACQUIRE_LOCK/RELEASE_LOCK and Py_BEGIN/END_ALLOW_THREADS have no counterpart."] [26 1 "//   - Deallocation: a finalizer (runtime.SetFinalizer) queues BZ2_bz*End and the frees on the library"] [27 1 "//     (clib.Lib.Defer), run before its next call under the GIL."] [39 1 "// bzlib.h's action and return codes."] [75 1 "// bzsOffsets are bz_stream's size and fields' offsets as the glue assumes them (pybz2_layout's order)."] [84 1 "// bz2 is the library's program, opened on the module's first use; its layout checked against the glue's."] [99 17 "// bz_stream *, C memory"] [106 27 "// bz_stream *, C memory"] [111 27 "// char *, C memory"] [113 2 "// bzs->avail_in is only 32 bit, so we store the true length separately. Conversion and looping is"] [114 2 "// encapsulated in decompress_buf()"] [120 1 "// The stream's fields."] [129 1 "// newStream is a zeroed bz_stream (bzalloc, bzfree and opaque NULL: libbzip2's default allocator)."] [139 1 "// Blocks output buffer wrappers (pycore_blocks_output_buffer.h): the block sizes."] [143 1 "// _BlocksOutputBuffer: the finished blocks' bytes in Go, the current block in C memory."] [146 19 "// the current block, C memory"] [153 1 "// OutputBuffer_InitAndGrow: the first block, max_length's when smaller; next_out and avail_out set."] [183 1 "// flushBlock copies the current block's bytes before avail_out into data and frees it."] [194 1 "// OutputBuffer_Grow: the next block (its size the table's, max_length's rest when smaller); -1 on failure."] [229 1 "// OutputBuffer_GetDataSize: the bytes written so far."] [234 1 "// OutputBuffer_Finish: the bytes object."] [240 1 "// OutputBuffer_OnError frees the current block."] [248 1 "/* Helper functions. */"] [250 1 "// catch_bz2_error gives the exception for an error code, nil for a success."] [274 1 "// cbytes is a copy of data in C memory (malloc'd; 0 for no bytes), the Py_buffer libbzip2 reads."] [287 1 "/* BZ2Compressor class. */"] [300 3 "/* On a 64-bit system, len might not fit in avail_in (an unsigned int). Do compression in chunks of no\n\t\t   more than UINT_MAX bytes each. */"] [306 3 "/* In regular compression mode, stop when input data is exhausted. */"] [321 3 "/* In flushing mode, stop when all buffered data has been flushed. */"] [374 1 "/* BZ2Decompressor class. */"] [376 1 "/*\nDecompress data of length d->bzs_avail_in_real in d->bzs.next_in. The output buffer is allocated dynamically\n\n\tand returned. At most max_length bytes are returned, so some of the input may not be consumed.\n\td->bzs.next_in and d->bzs_avail_in_real are updated to reflect the consumed input.\n*/"] [390 3 "/* On a 64-bit system, buffer length might not fit in avail_out, so we do decompression in chunks of no\n\t\t   more than UINT_MAX bytes each. Note that the expression for `avail` is guaranteed to be positive, so\n\t\t   the cast is safe. */"] [425 23 "// the caller's buffer in C memory (freed at the end)"] [427 2 "/* Prepend unconsumed input if necessary */"] [429 3 "/* Number of bytes we can append to input buffer */"] [432 3 "/* Number of bytes we can append if we move existing contents to beginning of buffer (overwriting\n\t\t   consumed input) */"] [440 4 "/* Assign to temporary variable first, so we don't lose address of allocated buffer if realloc\n\t\t\t   fails */"] [450 66 "// memmove"] [484 3 "/* If we did not use the input buffer, we now have to copy the tail from the caller's buffer into the\n\t\t   input buffer */"] [488 4 "/* Discard buffer if it's too small (resizing it may needlessly copy the current contents) */"] [494 4 "/* Allocate if necessary */"] [504 4 "/* Copy tail */"] [505 66 "// memcpy"] [516 3 "// Re-entering BZ2_bzDecompress() after an error can write out of bounds."] [544 1 "/* Module initialization. */"] [550 3 "// a C type's instance with state and no __getstate__ (object_getstate): \"cannot pickle 'TP_NAME' object\""] [641 1 "// methO checks a METH_O method's one argument (args[0] is self)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[89 46] [317 37] [360 36] [397 35] [529 36] [571 46] [578 40]]} (go/file "pybz2.go" :imports [

    ;; _bz2module.c: Copyright (c) the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License Agreement for Python 3.14
    ;; (LICENSE.md). The port to Go: Copyright (c) the Arbace authors, under the same license.

    ;; The module _bz2 (queue 208; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 208"; PYS22 (a)): CPython 3.14.10's
    ;; Modules/_bz2module.c (with Modules/clinic/_bz2module.c.h's argument parsing) ported statement for statement over
    ;; libbzip2 1.0.8 itself, the C library built by ci's builder (arbace/clib/bzip2's node program) and called through
    ;; arbace/clib: BZ2Compressor (compress, flush) and BZ2Decompressor (decompress with max_length, eof, unused_data,
    ;; needs_input). bz2.py, BZ2File and bz2.open are the tarball's Python over it. Its C names are kept (compress,
    ;; decompress_buf, decompress, catch_bz2_error, the _impl functions).
    ;;
    ;; How the C maps onto Go here:
    ;;
    ;;   - The bz_stream and the decompressor's input buffer are C memory in the library's program (malloc'd there);
    ;;     the stream's fields are read and written at their offsets, which the C side's pybz2_layout gives and the
    ;;     glue checks once (bzsLayout). A Py_buffer's bytes are copied into C memory for the call (data), as the
    ;;     caller's buffer CPython hands to libbzip2 directly.
    ;;   - The output buffer (_BlocksOutputBuffer, pycore_blocks_output_buffer.h) is C memory of one block at a
    ;;     time: each block's bytes are copied out to Go when the next is allocated and at the end, so the block
    ;;     sizes libbzip2 sees (and so its calls) are CPython's.
    ;;   - bzalloc/bzfree are NULL: libbzip2's default allocator, musl's malloc in the program (CPython's
    ;;     BZ2_Malloc/BZ2_Free are PyMem_RawMalloc/Free; the difference is invisible to Python).
    ;;   - Locks: the caller holds pyi's GIL around every call (the library's one C thread is shared), so
    ;;     ACQUIRE_LOCK/RELEASE_LOCK and Py_BEGIN/END_ALLOW_THREADS have no counterpart.
    ;;   - Deallocation: a finalizer (runtime.SetFinalizer) queues BZ2_bz*End and the frees on the library
    ;;     (clib.Lib.Defer), run before its next call under the GIL.


    ^{:go/apos {1 [30 2]} :go/pos {:lparen [29 8] :rparen [35 1] :tok-pos [29 1]}} [runtime "runtime"]

